			<!-- PRE-BOOK MENTION: READ BEFORE CHAPTER ONE (Page iv) -->
			<section class="book-page" id="expectation">
				<div class="page-body-content">
					<div class="page-running-head">
						<span class="chapter-header-label">Decoding the Burn</span>
						<span class="page-count-label">Preliminary &bull; Page iv</span>
					</div>

					<h2 class="chapter-title" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Expectations: What You Can Expect from This&nbsp;Book</h2>

					<div class="chapter-content is-first-page">
						<p>Burning Mouth Syndrome has multiple root causes. This book is specifically about the acid-triggered type, which I discovered through my own personal journey. I do not yet know how many people this mechanism applies to, and we still need significantly more clinical research to understand the true proportion of patients who can be helped. Acid-driven burning mouth is something that can be tested through a temporary low-acid or no-acid diet, but I do not know if it is going to work for every single&nbsp;reader.</p>
						<p>Depending on where you are in your journey, you might have high expectations or very low expectations. Both reactions are completely normal. Every case is distinct, and this book should be viewed as an investigative N=1 case study from which you can learn and test hypotheses for your own&nbsp;situation.</p>
						<p>I understand what you are going through: the sleepless nights, the anxiety, and the exhaustion of having dentists and doctors tell you that everything looks fine while your mouth feels like it is on fire. Early on, I realized certain everyday inputs made my pain dramatically worse, while others allowed it to calm down. That is the core purpose of this book: not promising an overnight cure, but finding practical ways to lower your pain to the minimum. And even if it does not work for you, at least you will have eliminated a major variable from your&nbsp;search.</p>
						<p>Achieving relief often requires modifying daily habits: what we eat, what we drink, how we brush, and how we collaborate with dentists on microscopic restoration margins or exposed root surfaces. That can take real money and out-of-pocket costs for specialized dental evaluations and repairs. I know this path demands a huge expenditure of energy, finances, time, and emotional vulnerability. I deeply respect that&nbsp;investment.</p>
						<p>My ultimate goal is to share these discoveries so that some patients can find relief right now, while sparking broader clinical research that eventually helps many more. By working through this book, you will gain undeniable clarity over your personal triggers: what makes your pain better, and what makes it&nbsp;worse.</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="page-number-footer">
					<span>iv</span>
				</div>
			</section>

			<!-- CONTRIBUTORS DIRECTORY: PAGE 1 (Page v) -->
			<section class="book-page" id="contributors">
				<div class="page-body-content">
					<div class="page-running-head">
						<span class="chapter-header-label">Decoding the Burn</span>
						<span class="page-count-label">Patient Research &bull; Page v</span>
					</div>

					<h2 class="chapter-title" style="margin-top: 1rem;">Contribute as a Patient to the&nbsp;Research</h2>

					<div class="chapter-content">
						<p style="font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.78; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; text-wrap: pretty;">
							Burning Mouth Syndrome has remained an unresolved puzzle for decades because patient data is rarely collected, organized, and analyzed in one place. <em>Decoding the Burn</em> is a patient-led, open citizen science initiative to gather real-world observations on oral acidity, dentin permeability, and trigeminal pain&nbsp;pathways.
						</p>

						<p style="font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.78; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; text-wrap: pretty;">
							To make this research truly useful, we need to collect patient stories from both sides: successful journeys and non-successful trials. If you tested a low-acid diet, removed chemical irritants, or sealed exposed root margins and experienced relief, your experience helps validate key mechanisms. But just as importantly, if you tried these protocols and nothing changed, that data is equally critical. In clinical science, knowing what fails helps rule out variables and proves that different biological mechanisms are at play for different&nbsp;individuals.
						</p>

						<p style="font-size: 1.08rem; line-height: 1.78; color: #1e293b; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; text-wrap: pretty;">
							Whether your experience was a complete success, a partial improvement, or produced zero difference, sharing your timeline, known triggers, and dental history provides vital evidence. By combining collective patient experiences, we can help build the empirical foundation needed for future clinical&nbsp;trials.
						</p>

						<p style="font-size: 1.05rem; line-height: 1.72; color: #0f172a; margin-top: 2rem; text-wrap: pretty;">
							To share your patient story and contribute your data, please reach out directly at <strong>decodingtheburn.com/contact</strong> or connect through our citizen science&nbsp;portal.
						</p>
					</div>
				</div>

				<div class="page-number-footer">
					<span>v</span>
