					<h2 class="chapter-title" style="margin-top: 0.75rem; margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">Executive Summary: Overview &amp; Foundations</h2>

					<div class="chapter-content">
						<div class="exec-summary-wrap">
							<p class="exec-lead-paragraph">
								Burning mouth pain, or generalized oral pain where the gums, tongue, lips, and palate burn relentlessly, is often diagnosed as Burning Mouth Syndrome (BMS) once clinical tests return normal and other variables are eliminated. It presents an exhausting clinical puzzle because standard visual examinations of the oral mucosa reveal completely healthy-looking tissue. While chronic oral burning can involve complex neurological, systemic, and neuropathic factors, my own eighteen-month investigation narrowed down oral acidity and Acid-Sensing Ion Channels (ASICs) as the primary peripheral drivers at play. This book documents that research, providing an observational, first-principles framework to help patients and clinicians investigate chemical triggers and microscopic dental pathways alongside established medical&nbsp;care.
							</p>

							<div class="exec-section-card">
								<h3 class="exec-card-title">Part I: Understanding Burning Mouth Syndrome &amp; History</h3>
								<p class="exec-card-text">
									Epidemiological realities (over 80 million sufferers worldwide, 3:1 to 5:1 female ratio), daily symptom characteristics across the tongue, palate, and lips, and the crushing human toll of the 3-to-5 doctor diagnostic odyssey. Crucially, this part traces the 70-year history from psychiatric dismissal to Lauria's 2005 small-fiber biopsy proof of denuded axonal sprouts, culminating in the modern 2026 international diagnostic&nbsp;consensus.
								</p>
							</div>

							<div class="exec-section-card">
								<h3 class="exec-card-title">Part II: My Story (An N=1 Investigation)</h3>
								<p class="exec-card-text">
									A software engineer's chronological case history documenting a sudden 10/10 burning pain flare triggered by acidic craft beer and wine. It details clean radiographs, 50+ failed supplements, the discovery of the carnivore elimination trial (starving oral bacteria to halt lactic acid), identifying the 48-to-72-hour delayed latency wave, the 92-dentist clinical poll, Crown #19 micro-leakage, and immediate relief from Gluma tubule&nbsp;desensitizers.
								</p>
							</div>

							<div class="exec-section-card">
								<h3 class="exec-card-title">Part III: The First Principles of Oral Burning Pain</h3>
								<p class="exec-card-text">
									The biophysical hardware and receptor physiology driving the burn. We examine why ambient acidity denatures tissue barriers and how Acid-Sensing Ion Channels (ASIC1 and ASIC3) fire relentless pain at pH below 6.8 without desensitizing. We detail 2-micron crown margin micro-leakage, the masticatory capillary pump, exposed dentinal tubule hydrodynamics, and the V3 trigeminal convergence circuit in the&nbsp;brainstem.
								</p>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

