							<p class="stat-page-desc">
								When patients rate their burning on a standard 0-to-10 visual pain scale, the average score is an agonizing 7.2 out of 10 (&plusmn;1.8) (Granot & Nagler, 2005; Scala et al., 2003). Standardized hospital metrics (McGill Pain Questionnaire) rank chronic oral burning alongside renal colic (kidney stones), acute herpes zoster (shingles), and severe sciatica. It is not mild irritation; it is severe, unrelenting physical&nbsp;pain.
							</p>
