							<p class="stat-page-desc">
								A multi-center survey (Klasser et al., 2011; Kohorst et al., 2014) documented that patients consult an average of 4.1 healthcare providers (general dentists, periodontists, endodontists, ENT specialists, and neurologists) across a span of 26.4 months (over two years) before receiving an official diagnosis. Because oral mucosa appears completely normal on visual inspection, 71% of patients report being told their oral tissues show no visible cause for&nbsp;pain.
