							<h1 class="stat-page-number">74% Triggered by Acid</h1>
							<h2 class="stat-page-title">Dietary Acid Sparks the Fire: Coffee, Wine, Citrus &amp;&nbsp;Vinegar</h2>
							<p class="stat-page-desc">
								In a structured clinical intake poll of 77 consecutive individuals tracking chemical flare triggers, 74.0% (57 of 77 participants) documented acute pain intensification following the intake of acidic beverages or foods, including coffee (pH 4.8 to 5.2), citrus fruits (pH 3.0 to 3.8), wine (pH 3.2 to 3.6), vinegar dressings, and carbonated beverages. Free hydrogen ions (H<sup>+</sup>) in acidic consumables directly open acid-sensing ion channels (ASIC1, ASIC3, and TRPV1) on sensitized oral nerve&nbsp;endings.
							</p>
							<div class="stat-page-source">
