					<div class="chapter-content is-first-page" style="max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto;">
						<p style="font-size: 1.18rem; line-height: 1.85; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; text-indent: 0; color: #1e293b;">
							Behind every epidemiological statistic and clinical diagnosis are real human beings whose lives have been upended by chronic oral pain. Burning Mouth Syndrome does not just burn the tongue; it disrupts sleep, strains relationships, turns everyday meals into anxious calculations, and isolates individuals inside a relentless physical sensation that no one around them can&nbsp;see.
						</p>
						<p style="font-size: 1.14rem; line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 1.5rem; text-indent: 0; color: #334155;">
							Here are stories from real people across the world documenting what it truly feels like to live with this condition: how the fire started without warning, the profound frustration of spotless clinical exams, and the quiet resilience required to keep searching for answers when conventional pathways offer little&nbsp;clarity.
						</p>
