						<p>This highlights a significant structural boundary in modern healthcare: dentistry focuses primarily on hard tissue pathology (caries, fractures) and periodontal attachment, while neurology focuses on central pain processing. Peripheral micro-chemical leaks at the tooth-mucosa margin sit directly at the intersection of both disciplines. Recognizing this interface creates an essential bridge, allowing dentists and physicians to combine restorative sealing with neurological support for comprehensive patient&nbsp;care.</p>
