						<!-- Section: Official ICOP Diagnostic Criteria & Clinical Workup Sequence -->
						<div id="ch19-icop-criteria" class="quiz-book-card" style="margin-bottom: 1.25rem; padding: 1.15rem 1.35rem; background: #f8fafc; border: 1.5px solid #cbd5e1; border-radius: 10px;">
							<h3 style="font-size: 1.05rem; font-weight: 700; color: #1e293b; margin: 0 0 0.5rem; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem;">
								<span>Official ICOP Diagnostic Criteria &amp; Clinical Workup&nbsp;Sequence</span>
							</h3>
							<p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #475569; line-height: 1.55; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">
								Under the <strong>International Classification of Orofacial Pain (ICOP 2020 &sect;6.1)</strong> and the <strong>International Classification of Headache Disorders (ICHD-3)</strong>, Burning Mouth Syndrome is defined by strict operational criteria. It is a formal diagnosis of exclusion requiring systematic verification that visible mucosal lesions, local dental etiologies, and systemic medical diseases are ruled&nbsp;out:
							</p>

							<!-- Part 1: Core ICOP Diagnostic Criteria (Check all that apply) -->
							<div style="background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.85rem 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">
								<h4 style="font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; margin: 0 0 0.45rem;">1. Core ICOP Diagnostic Criteria (Check all that apply to your symptoms)</h4>
								<div class="bms-grid-1col" style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #1e293b; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.45rem;">
									<label class="bms-check-label">
										<input type="checkbox" name="icop_daily_recurrence" class="bms-input-persist" />
										<span><strong>Criterion A &amp; B (Duration &amp; Frequency):</strong> Burning or dysaesthetic sensation recurring daily for &gt;2 hours per day for &gt;3 continuous&nbsp;months.</span>
									</label>
									<label class="bms-check-label">
										<input type="checkbox" name="icop_burning_quality" class="bms-input-persist" />
										<span><strong>Criterion C (Sensory Quality):</strong> Pain has a distinct burning, scalding, or raw sensation felt superficially within the oral&nbsp;mucosa.</span>
									</label>
									<label class="bms-check-label">
										<input type="checkbox" name="icop_normal_mucosa" class="bms-input-persist" />
										<span><strong>Criterion D1 (Normal Clinical Appearance):</strong> Clinical visual examination confirms healthy, intact pink mucosa with zero ulcerations or visible&nbsp;inflammation.</span>
									</label>
									<label class="bms-check-label">
										<input type="checkbox" name="icop_taste_dryness" class="bms-input-persist" />
										<span><strong>Associated Features:</strong> Accompanied by subjective dry mouth sensation (xerostomia) or altered taste (dysgeusia: persistent metallic or salty&nbsp;taste).</span>
									</label>
								</div>
							</div>

							<!-- Part 2: Local Dental & Oral Medicine Exclusion Checklist -->
							<div style="background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.85rem 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">
								<h4 style="font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; margin: 0 0 0.35rem;">2. Local Dental &amp; Mucosal Exclusion Sequence (Check tests completed)</h4>
								<p style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #64748b; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">International guidelines require ruling out primary intraoral causes before confirming idiopathic BMS:</p>
								<div class="bms-grid-2col" style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #1e293b;">
									<label class="bms-check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="icop_test_candida" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span><strong>Oral Lesion / Candida Smear:</strong> Swab or culture ruling out fungal overgrowth, lichen planus, or leukoplakia.</span></label>
									<label class="bms-check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="icop_test_sialometry" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span><strong>Quantitative Sialometry:</strong> Flow measurement ruling out objective hyposalivation (&lt;0.1 mL/min resting).</span></label>
									<label class="bms-check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="icop_test_bewe" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span><strong>BEWE Diagnostic Score (Erosive Wear):</strong> Basic Erosive Wear Examination (BEWE) scoring 0–3 to evaluate chemical enamel dissolution &amp; exposed dentin.</span></label>
									<label class="bms-check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="icop_test_prosthetic" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span><strong>Prosthetic &amp; Mechanical Audit:</strong> Evaluation of denture stability, sharp cusps, or restoration friction.</span></label>
									<label class="bms-check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="icop_test_patch" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span><strong>Dental Patch Testing:</strong> Epicutaneous allergy screen for metals, acrylates, gold, or flavoring agents.</span></label>
									<label class="bms-check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="icop_test_galvanic" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span><strong>Galvanic Current Check:</strong> Audit of dissimilar intraoral restorative metals in saliva.</span></label>
									<label class="bms-check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="icop_test_margins" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span><strong>High-Magnification Margin Loupe Exam:</strong> Inspection of crown margins and receded roots for micro-leakage.</span></label>
								</div>
							</div>

							<!-- Part 3: Systemic Medical Laboratory Exclusion Checklist -->
							<div style="background: #ffffff; border: 1px solid #e2e8f0; border-radius: 8px; padding: 0.85rem 1rem; margin-bottom: 0.65rem;">
								<h4 style="font-size: 0.88rem; font-weight: 700; color: #0f172a; margin: 0 0 0.35rem;">3. Systemic Medical Laboratory Exclusion Sequence (Check panels completed)</h4>
								<p style="font-size: 0.78rem; color: #64748b; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">Standard laboratory blood panels to identify or rule out secondary systemic drivers:</p>
								<div class="bms-grid-2col" style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #1e293b;">
									<label class="bms-check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="icop_lab_hematinic" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span><strong>Hematinic &amp; Vitamin Panel:</strong> CBC, Ferritin, Serum B12, RBC Folate, Serum Zinc, and Vitamin D.</span></label>
									<label class="bms-check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="icop_lab_glycemic" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span><strong>Glycemic Screening:</strong> Fasting blood glucose and HbA1c to rule out diabetic small-fiber neuropathy.</span></label>
									<label class="bms-check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="icop_lab_thyroid" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span><strong>Endocrine / Thyroid Profile:</strong> Serum TSH, Free T3, and Free T4 for subclinical thyroid dysfunction.</span></label>
									<label class="bms-check-label"><input type="checkbox" name="icop_lab_autoimmune" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span><strong>Autoimmune Serology:</strong> ANA, Anti-SSA (Ro), and Anti-SSB (La) to rule out Sj&ouml;gren's syndrome.</span></label>
									<label class="bms-check-label" style="grid-column: 1 / -1;"><input type="checkbox" name="icop_lab_medication" class="bms-input-persist" /> <span><strong>Pharmacotherapy Audit:</strong> Medication review ruling out ACE inhibitor or ARB-induced secondary burning.</span></label>
								</div>
							</div>

							<!-- Interactive Blog Link -->
							<p style="font-size: 0.82rem; color: #4338ca; margin: 0.65rem 0 0; line-height: 1.5;">
