					<div class="chapter-content">
						<h3>What Happens Over the 14 Days on Zero-Acid</h3>
						<p>Once you strip away all external dietary acids and fermentable carbohydrates, your oral nervous system and subgingival biofilm undergo a predictable biological de-escalation&nbsp;sequence:</p>

						<p><strong>Days 1 to 2 (Starvation of the Biofilm):</strong> External dietary acids stop entering the mouth. Without starches or simple sugars, oral biofilm bacteria (<em>Streptococcus mutans</em>) are deprived of the substrate needed to produce lactic acid.</p>

						<p><strong>Days 3 to 5 (Extracellular Proton Clearance):</strong> Local bacterial lactic, acetic, and propionic acid production collapses toward zero. Gingival sulcus pH rises from an acidic 4.5-5.5 back toward a neutral 7.0-7.4. Free hydrogen protons (H<sup>+</sup>) clear from extracellular fluid, allowing Acid-Sensing Ion Channels (specifically ASIC1 and ASIC3) and TRPV1 receptors to lock into their closed, resting&nbsp;state.</p>

						<p><strong>Days 6 to 10 (Neural De-escalation):</strong> The continuous volley of high-frequency action potentials traveling up the Trigeminal Nerve subsides. Second-order relay neurons in the brainstem Subnucleus Caudalis drop out of hyperexcitable central&nbsp;sensitization.</p>

						<p><strong>Days 11 to 14 (Deep Baseline Stabilization):</strong> Frayed mucosal tissues enter deep physiological rest. Severe burning scores typically plunge from an agonizing 8-10/10 down to a calm 1-3/10 or complete, quiet&nbsp;silence.</p>

						<h3>Immediate Post-Meal Neutralization: The Warm Bicarbonate Protocol</h3>
						<p>Even on an ultra-low-acid baseline, natural meal mastication, salivary shifts, and trace organic compounds can disturb compromised oral surfaces. Standard water lacks the buffering capacity to instantly neutralize subgingival micro-pH. To guarantee chemical silence, deploy the <strong>Warm Sodium Bicarbonate Rinse</strong> after every single meal:</p>
						<ol class="chapter-list">
							<li>Dissolve 1/2 teaspoon of pure sodium bicarbonate (baking soda) in 4 ounces of lukewarm water.</li>
							<li>Gently swish the alkaline solution across your teeth and gums for 30 to 45 seconds, ensuring the fluid circulates into posterior gingival margins.</li>
							<li>Spit gently without rinsing with plain water, allowing a micro-thin alkaline buffer to coat the teeth and neutralize residual hydrogen ions.</li>
						</ol>
					</div>
				</div>

