					<div class="chapter-content">
						<h3>Stepping Down: What to Do If Low-Acid Isn't Enough</h3>
						<p>If you complete 10 to 14 days on the Gentle Low-Acid Trial and your burning pain drops noticeably, you have confirmed that acid is your primary trigger. However, what if you still experience a lingering smolder or persistent 4-6/10 pain?</p>

						<p><strong>The Stepped De-escalation Protocol:</strong><br />
						If low-acid whole foods do not fully silence the fire, your nerve tripwires may be hyper-sensitized to even trace plant organic acids or subgingival fermentation. The solution is simple: drop the tofu, drop the vegetables, avocado, and mushrooms, and transition to <strong>Option 1 (pure meat, fish, eggs, and water)</strong> for another one to two weeks. Stripping away the remaining plant compounds allows you to test whether pure zero-acid is required to achieve complete pain-free baseline&nbsp;stability.</p>

						<h3>Strategic Real-World Cycles</h3>
						<p>Neither trial is intended as lifelong deprivation. Once your nerve alarm quietens and your baseline drops, you can utilize flexible hybrid rhythms:</p>

						<p><strong>1. The 5+1 Single-Meal Challenge:</strong> Follow five days of strict zero-acid carnivore (Monday through Friday) to lock oral pH at neutral. On Saturday, introduce a single low-acid meal (such as grilled salmon with steamed zucchini and avocado). Sunday returns to baseline. This isolates delayed reactions within the 48-to-72-hour latency window.</p>

						<p><strong>2. The 5+2 Weekend Rhythm:</strong> Follow zero-acid animal baseline during the working week, shifting to low-acid whole foods on weekends to accommodate family dining while maintaining clinical control.</p>

