					<div class="chapter-content">
						<p>To eliminate guesswork and prove whether acidity is actively powering your pain circuit, you must measure the delayed curve using a controlled mathematical delta. Here is the step-by-step calculation framework:</p>

						<div class="timelag-box">
							<p class="timelag-title">The Core 3-Day Off / 3-Day On Delta Calculation Protocol</p>
							<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #334155; margin-bottom: 0.85rem;">
								Select ONE suspect variable: <strong>Acidic Drinks</strong> (coffee, citrus juice, soda, tea, vinegar, sparkling water). Keep everything else in your routine strictly stable.
							</p>

							<table class="timelag-table">
								<thead>
									<tr>
										<th>Day</th>
										<th>Action / Status</th>
										<th>Expected Pain (0-10)</th>
										<th>Biological Explanation</th>
									</tr>
								</thead>
								<tbody>
									<tr>
										<td><strong>Day 1 (Hold)</strong></td>
										<td>Zero acidic drinks; room-temp water only</td>
										<td>High (~8.0 / 10)</td>
										<td>Residual 48-hour fermentation wave from prior days is still firing.</td>
									</tr>
									<tr>
										<td><strong>Day 2 (Hold)</strong></td>
										<td>Zero acidic drinks; clean neutral hydration</td>
										<td>Dropping (~6.0 / 10)</td>
										<td>Subgingival acid wash begins diluting; ASIC channels start repolarizing.</td>
									</tr>
									<tr>
										<td><strong>Day 3 (Hold)</strong></td>
										<td>Zero acidic drinks; stable baseline</td>
										<td>Low Point (~3.5 / 10)</td>
										<td><strong>Baseline Score (B):</strong> The un-fueled state. Tissue inflammation settles.</td>
									</tr>
									<tr>
										<td><strong>Day 4 (Trial)</strong></td>
										<td>Reintroduce 1-2 cups of the suspect drink</td>
										<td>Deceptive (~4.0 / 10)</td>
										<td>False comfort. Initial ingestion feels fine; the slow fuse is quietly lit.</td>
									</tr>
									<tr>
										<td><strong>Day 5 (Trial)</strong></td>
										<td>Continue 1-2 cups of suspect drink daily</td>
										<td>Surging (~6.5 / 10)</td>
										<td>Bacterial lactic acid production ramps up in open tubule collars.</td>
									</tr>
									<tr>
										<td><strong>Day 6 (Trial)</strong></td>
										<td>Continue suspect drink</td>
										<td>Peak (~8.5 / 10)</td>
										<td><strong>Challenge Peak (C):</strong> Full delayed ASIC proton overdrive achieved.</td>
									</tr>
								</tbody>
