							<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #334155; margin-bottom: 0.4rem;">
								<strong>The Lag Delta Formula:</strong>
							</p>
							<div class="formula-badge">
								Lag Delta (&Delta;) = Average Pain (Days 5 and 6) - Baseline Pain (Day 3)
							</div>
							<p style="font-size: 0.84rem; line-height: 1.5; color: #475569; margin-top: 0.4rem; margin-bottom: 0;">
								<strong>Score Interpretation:</strong> If &Delta; is <strong>+2.0 or greater</strong>, you have definitive clinical confirmation: dietary acid is an active electrochemical fuel powering your oral circuit.
							</p>
						</div>

						<h3>Three Alternative Testing and Verification Protocols</h3>

						<div class="alt-protocol-card">
							<p class="alt-protocol-title">Alternative 1: The Single Pulse Spike (Fast Weekend Test)</p>
							<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #334155; margin: 0;">
								If you cannot endure three consecutive days of pain flares, use the single pulse method. Establish a neutral baseline Monday through Thursday. On Friday morning at 8:00 AM, drink ONE single 8oz glass of orange juice or black coffee. Immediately return to zero-acid water for the entire weekend. Record your pain every 12 hours. Look for the distinctive bell curve: flat on Friday, beginning to sting Saturday evening, peaking Sunday at 48 hours, and returning to calm by Monday afternoon. This pinpoints your exact personal latency hours down to the clock.
							</p>
						</div>

						<div class="alt-protocol-card">
							<p class="alt-protocol-title">Alternative 2: The Split A/B Rotation Block (12-Day Wave Verification)</p>
							<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #334155; margin: 0;">
								For skeptical clinicians or family members who assume your pain is psychosomatic, execute a 12-day split block: 3 Days OFF &rarr; 3 Days ON &rarr; 3 Days OFF &rarr; 3 Days ON. Graphing daily pain levels over twelve days reveals an undeniable oscillating sine wave shifted exactly 48 to 72 hours behind your intake ledger. A repeating biological wave disproves placebo, stress, or random fluctuation with mathematical certainty.
							</p>
						</div>

						<div class="alt-protocol-card" style="margin-bottom: 0;">
							<p class="alt-protocol-title">Alternative 3: The Mechanical Barrier Straw Test (Hardware vs. Systemic)</p>
							<p style="font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.55; color: #334155; margin: 0;">
								Wondering if the acid is irritating a stomach nerve reflex or directly penetrating a leaking tooth margin? Coat your suspected tooth crown or receded root neck with orthodontic dental wax, or insert a custom night barrier tray. Drink the acidic beverage through a straw aimed towards the back of the throat, avoiding contact with the shielded tooth. If the 48-hour burning surge fails to appear, you have conclusively isolated the culprit: the trigger is a direct physical hardware leak, not a systemic or central brain defect.
							</p>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

