						<h3>Why Other In-Office Desensitizers Fail for Burning Mouth</h3>
						<p>Many sufferers receive in-office desensitizers that provide zero relief. Reviewing clinical records usually reveals an entirely different chemical class that fails to block peripheral acid ingress:</p>

						<ul>
							<li><strong>Why X-PUR Crystal does NOT work:</strong> X-PUR Crystal relies on potassium oxalate to precipitate loose calcium oxalate salt crystals at the tubule entrance. Because these crystals are extremely superficial and dissolve rapidly in acidic oral environments (dietary acids, coffee, or bacterial lactic acid), the seal breaks down within days. Furthermore, oxalate salts require bare tooth calcium to precipitate, meaning they cannot bond to old composite or crown margins.</li>
							<li><strong>Why Silver Diamine Fluoride (SDF) does NOT work:</strong> Formulated as an antimicrobial caries arrester rather than a sealed neuropathic barrier. SDF creates discontinuous silver salt precipitates that leave gaps for microscopic hydrogen ions (H<sup>+</sup>) to enter, while permanently staining demineralized root margins jet black without silencing the pain.</li>
						</ul>
